# audit2.bcyr — benchmarks of the library-wide overflow audit from its B5 on (ADR 0002 #35 …), Cyrius-only, as
# tests/audit.bcyr's are for B1–B4 (ADR 0002 #27 … #34): the functions each batch fixed, on typical inputs and on the
# edges that take their other paths. With B5's benches tests/audit.bcyr would take about 219 s of `cyrius bench`'s
# 300 s per-file deadline (189 s without), so the audit's later batches open this third file, the same way B4 split
# tests/kimiya.bcyr (the user's decision of 2026-11-11: split the bench files rather than raise the deadline). The
# method is kimiya.bcyr's: each timed batch is a tight loop of `per_batch` calls, inputs from globals (Rust's
# `black_box`), results to a sink.

include "src/error.cyr"
include "src/constants.cyr"
include "src/mathx_data.cyr"
include "src/mathx.cyr"
include "src/validate.cyr"
include "src/element_data.cyr"
include "src/element.cyr"
